#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""phone-hub: a phone-sized view of your workmux agents, served privately over your tailnet. It can read their screens, send them
typed replies, press keys in their dialogs, and show a diff or an artifact for annotation. Everything that types into an agent is
behind the PIN, a preview or confirm step, and rate limits (agents may run with permissions bypassed).

  phone-hub serve            run the server (127.0.0.1 only; `tailscale serve` publishes it on the tailnet)
  phone-hub ensure           start it detached if it is not answering (idempotent; tmux.conf calls this); it runs under
                             a small supervisor that starts the server again if it ever dies
  phone-hub restart          stop the server; the supervisor starts it again with the code on disk
  phone-hub supervise        the restart loop itself (started by ensure; you do not run this)
  phone-hub set-pin          set the login PIN (run it in YOUR terminal; it prompts, nothing is echoed)
  phone-hub pair             print a one-time code that pairs ONE phone (valid 10 minutes)
  phone-hub devices          list paired devices
  phone-hub revoke ID        unpair a device (and end its sessions)
  phone-hub off | on         kill switch: everything except /healthz answers 503 while it is off
  phone-hub status           what is running, what is configured
  phone-hub log [-n N]       last audit log lines
  phone-hub selftest         read the agent list and one pane from THIS environment (no content printed)

Design and threat model: ~/.local/share/general/plan-b-hub-v1-design.md. In short, every request must pass, in order:
Host header, Tailscale identity header, device cookie (pairing), PIN session. Pane text is untrusted and always escaped;
there is no JavaScript. Anything that types into an agent additionally needs a fresh PIN, a one-use preview, and a check that the
screen still shows what you saw.

First run: put your Tailscale login and this machine's tailnet name in config.json as "login" and "host" (no defaults: the hub refuses to start without them).
Files: ~/.config/phone-hub/ (config.json, secrets.json mode 600) and ~/.local/state/phone-hub/ (audit.log, server.log, disabled).
"""
